    "text": "Let <math><mi>l</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> intersects the parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math> at points <math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If <math><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></math> meet the parabola again at <math><mi>R</mi></math> and <math><mi>T</mi></math> respectively (where <math><mi>S</mi></math> is the focus of <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;), then the slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
